  "notes": "GAAP. Receipts/disbursements from Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p4), Total Governmental Funds column. No debt proceeds on that statement (warrant issuance appears only on the budgetary schedules p5-6, budgetary basis). Taxes assessed treated as property tax; the district reports no special assessment revenue. Balance sheet uses the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1); warrants payable (no due-date split) put in debt - due in more than one year per the SID rule. Beginning cash not shown; ending_cash = cash on deposit with County Treasurer from governmental funds balance sheet (p3). Detail comes from the budget-to-actual schedules (budgetary basis actuals, which differ from the GAAP statement; fund lines are not on any more detailed schedule). Pay/paying agent fees categorised as debt interest and fees. Read pages 1-6 of 6."
